    {
      "id": "7b399c7b-c324-4e98-9232-dc7e08fec701",
      "name": "Sticky - sticky-main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1120,
        1520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#F9D348",
        "width": 540,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## **AI Competitor Change Tracker**\n\n**Who it's for:** Anyone who wants to monitor competitors without manually checking their websites \u2014 marketers, founders, agencies tracking clients' competitors.\n\n**What it does:** On a schedule, scrapes each competitor's website, has AI produce a full competitive intelligence report, logs it to Sheets, and emails you a polished PDF.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Reads your list of competitor URLs from Google Sheets\n2. Loops through each one and scrapes the site with Firecrawl\n3. AI analyzes positioning, messaging, trust signals, weaknesses, and more\n4. Logs a summary row to Google Sheets\n5. Builds a styled HTML report and converts it to PDF\n6. Emails you the PDF, then moves to the next competitor\n\n**How to set up**\n\u2610 Connect Firecrawl (Bearer Auth)\n\u2610 Connect OpenAI\n\u2610 Connect HTML2PDF (Header Auth)\n\u2610 Connect Google Sheets and select your own competitor list + log sheet\n\u2610 Connect Gmail and set your own recipient email\n\u2610 Set your own run interval on the Schedule Trigger\n\n**CUSTOMIZATION**\n- Change which fields the AI extracts (edit the output schema + prompt)\n- Adjust the HTML report's styling/branding\n- Run it more or less often depending on how fast competitors change"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
